From: txtyb <txtybbill@163.com>
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: oplus: AD296: ADFR tables and SA floor table

 arm64: dts: oplus: AD296 panel: ADFR tables and SA floor table

 * Restore the oplus,adfr-min-fps-mapping-table entries and command sequences
   for the 144 Hz and 165 Hz timings (LineageOS only ships three of them).
 * Add oplus,adfr-sa-min-fps-bl-table so the driver can pick the SA floor from
   the current backlight level.
 * Clear BIT14 of oplus,adfr-config so the SA mode is restored after boot.
 * Do NOT advertise qcom,dsi-qsync-mode-avr-step-fps: that turns on ARR, which
   keeps the display in a variable refresh state and stops the SoC from ever
   entering s2idle (measured: suspend success 0 vs 251 per five minutes).

--- a/qcom/display/oplus/panel/dsi-panel-AD296-P-3-A0020-dsc-cmd.dtsi
+++ b/qcom/display/oplus/panel/dsi-panel-AD296-P-3-A0020-dsc-cmd.dtsi
@@ -3150,11 +3150,13 @@
 	oplus,ofp-need-to-wait-data-before-aod-on;
 	oplus,ofp-aod-off-frame-cost = <1>;
 	/* adfr config */
-	oplus,adfr-config = <0x6e41>;  // 0b0110'1110'0100'0001
+	oplus,adfr-config = <0x2e41>;  // 0b0010'1110'0100'0001 -- BIT14(software marker) off so the TE GPIO irq is registered for real frame rate measurement
 	oplus,adfr-test-te-gpio = <&tlmm 85 0>;
 	/* just for qsync enable*/
 	qcom,qsync-enable;
-	qcom,mdss-dsi-qsync-min-refresh-rate = <30>;
+	qcom,mdss-dsi-qsync-min-refresh-rate = <1>;
+	/* backlight threshold and sa min fps pairs, highest threshold first, 0 keeps the mode rate */
+	oplus,adfr-sa-min-fps-bl-table = <1160 1>, <919 30>, <0 0>;
 
 	// qcom,dsi-dyn-clk-enable;
 
